<</Type/Catalog/Pages 1 0 R/Metadata 727 0 R/Lang(en)/StructTreeRoot 57 0 R/MarkInfo<</Marked true/Suspects false>>/ViewerPreferences<</Direction/L2R>>/Outlines 56 0 R/Names<</Dests<</Names[(boissin-e.-caparos-s.-de-neys-w.-2023.-no-easy-fix-for-belief-bias-during-syllogistic-reasoning-journal-of-cognitive-psychology.-httpsdoi.org10.108020445911.2023.2181734)584 0 R(effect-size)574 0 R(forced-delay-could-only-proceed-to-a-screen-registering-their-answer-after-a-certain-delay-which-varied-from-40-to-60-seconds-depending-on-the-word-count-of-the-vignettes.financial-incentive-double-compensation-to-think-things-through-in-detail-and-everyone-got-the-incentive-in-the-end.reasons-instructed-participants-that-they-would-have-to-provide-detailed-explanations-of-their-answers.crt-prime-complete-cognitive-reflection-test-before-the-vignette.)605 0 R(four-manipulations-on-thought-experiments-one-of-which-was-a-gettier-clock-case.)594 0 R(give-participants-a-3-paragraph-explanation-of-the-correct-and-lured-answers-and-the-relevance-of-the-base-rate.)594 0 R(give-participants-an-explanation-that-explicitly-stated-both-the-correct-response-and-the-typical-incorrect-response-after-each-belief-bias-problem-they-complete.)585 0 R(if-anything-2-and-3-led-people-to-judge-that-the-character-in-the-clock-case-knows-rather-than-philosophers-orthodox-answer.)607 0 R(improvement-in-correct-card-choices-compared-to-pre-intervention-choices)583 0 R(increase-in-correct-answers-compared-to-initial-responseson-belief-bias-problems-like-ours-where-believability-is-in-conflict-with-logical-validity-p.-18-see-also-figure-2-and-5.)586 0 R(intervention)573 0 R(introduce-participants-to-a-market-in-which-correct-wason-cards-receive-the-highest-payout-at-the-end-of-the-game-and-participants-can-see-the-price-for-each-card-they-carry-over-16-rounds-of-card-trading.)582 0 R(isler-o.-yilmaz-o.-2022.-how-to-activate-intuitive-and-reflective-thinking-in-behavior-research-a-comprehensive-examination-of-experimental-techniques.-behavior-research-methods.-httpsdoi.org10.3758s13428-022-01984-4)587 0 R<>593 0 R(materials)570 0 R(more-correct-final-responses-compared-to-initial-responses-in-training-group-figure-2)595 0 R(no-effect-of-1-4-on-gettier-response-distributions-compared-to-control.)595 0 R(participants-were-given-feedback-on-a-3-item-pre-test-of-1-the-semantic-illusion-2-the-base-rate-fallacy-and-3-the-availability-bias-and-after-each-question-on-the-correct-answer-together-with-a-detailed-explanation-of-the-biases-then-asked-to-write-four-sentences-summarizing-what-they-had-learned-in-the-training-and-were-finally-instructed-to-rely-on-reflection-a.k.a.-long-debiasing-training.-participants-then-took-the-aforesaid-reflection-test.force-participants-to-wait-at-least-10-seconds-to-give-a-final-response-after-giving-initial-response.41.5-improvement-relative-to-overall-control-conditions-in-average-number-of-correct-responsesnot-repeated-measure-within-participants-like-ours-but-a-single-response-between-participants-comparison0-between-participants-improvement-in-average-number-of-correct-responses-relative-to-overall-control-participants-but-30-within-participants-improvement-in-average-number-of-correct-responses-compared-to-initial-response-given-under-5s-time-pressure-so-the-within-participant-effect-shows-that-time-pressure-hinders-performance-not-that-delayed-responses-improve-performance.boissin-e.-caparos-s.-voudouri-a.-de-neys-w.-2022.-debiasing-system-1-training-favours-logical-over-stereotypical-intuiting.-judgment-and-decision-making-174-646690.-httpseconpapers.repec.orgarticlejdmjournlv_3a17_3ay_3a2022_3ai_3a4_3ap_3a646-690.htm)593 0 R(publication)572 0 R(section-10)590 0 R(section-11)591 0 R(section-12)592 0 R(section-13)596 0 R(section-14)597 0 R(section-15)595 0 R(section-16)598 0 R(section-17)601 0 R(section-18)602 0 R(section-19)603 0 R(section-2)571 0 R(section-20)604 0 R(section-21)606 0 R(section-3)575 0 R(section-4)576 0 R(section-5)577 0 R